WEBVTT

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.400
(traditional pop music
playing on speaker)

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.520
-(door opens) -(bell jingling)

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.160
(sighs)

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.280
Hey, we're...

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.640
Queenie.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.080
Hi, sweetie.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.440
(chuckles)

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.800
(Queenie chuckles)

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.440
Honey... (sighs)

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.120
...look at your bakery.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.160
It's like a ghost town.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.960
Yeah, well, I missed you.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.720
Oh, baby.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.280
Why don't you come here?

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.560
Come here.

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.360
(sniffles)

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:08.840
-(crying softly) -(Queenie) Hey.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.920
Everything's gonna be all right.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:19.040
Everything's gonna be just fine.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.600
(suspenseful music playing)

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:42.520
(whistling teasing tune)

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.960
Hey, sweetheart, what
brings you downtown?

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:52.440
I really hope you didn't spend
all day coming up with that.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.120
Oh, you want scary, is
that what you want?

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:01.840
You know what it is, you
just aren't menacing enough.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.600
(scoffing) I think
I'm plenty menacing.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.440
Am I not menacing?

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.280
Maybe if you waved your arms
around, you know, like a crazy
man,

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.720
then you'd appear more menacing.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:22.280
That's good. A little more.

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:26.720
A little more.

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.600
Keep going. Perfect.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:32.000
-(panting) -Three, two, one.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.040
Hey!

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.200
(metal clacking)

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.640
That's enough. Get outta here.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.560
What's on your mind, baker boy?

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:41.760
(Jacob) Ah, jeez.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:43.440
You should be ashamed of
yourselves.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:44.560
(man) Oh, well, we're not.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.000
(Jacob) It's a lady.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.360
(man scoffs)

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.400
I tell you what...

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:50.920
I'll give you the first shot.
Go ahead.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:51.960
You sure?

00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.320
(grunts) Oh, boy.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.760
-(body thuds) -(Jacob sighs)

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.200
(pan clatters)

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.280
Last time I ever help
that woman out again.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.360
Lally!

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.120
Whoopsie, Frank. Sometimes
I forget my own strength.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.440
I'll take it from here. Thank you!

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:11.400
Welcome.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:13.640
-(man) Catch you later, Lally.
-(Lally) Bye, Stanley.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:15.480
I'll be over for a game
of Befudler Dudley soon.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.200
-(Stanley) All right. -(chuckles)

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.600
That's my cousin Stanley.
He's a wizard.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:20.560
No.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.200
(Lally) Please! It's early,
don't make me work for it.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:24.520
I said I wanted out, and I want
out.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.640
Come now, Mr. Kowalski.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.080
Can't believe my therapist
said you wizards don't exist.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:30.400
(chuckles) What a waste of money!

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.680
You do know I'm a witch, right?

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:34.400
Yeah.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.920
-Look... -(tool clatters)

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.560
...you seem like a really nice
witch.

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.480
You don't know what I've been
through with you people.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.880
So, could you please
get out of my life?

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.840
-A little over a year ago...
-Oh, my...

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:48.440
...in the hopes of securing
a small business loan,

00:03:48.520 --> 00:03:50.440
you walked through the doors
of the Steen National Bank

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:52.800
located about six blocks from here.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.400
You then made the acquaintance
of Newt Scamander,

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:58.120
the world's foremost and,
albeit only, magizoologist.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.160
You then learned of a world

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:00.920
you had previously been
wholly unaware of.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.480
You met and fell in love with a
witch named Queenie Goldstein,

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.440
had your brain wiped by
means of Obliviation,

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:07.000
only it didn't take.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.880
And as a result, you
reunited with Ms.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:09.560
Goldstein who,

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.120
after your refusal to marry her,
mm,

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:15.800
decided to join Gellert Grindelwald
and his dark army of followers,

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.240
who pose the single greatest threat

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:19.880
to both your world and
ours in four centuries.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:21.440
How did I do?

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.880
(chuckles) That was good.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.080
Except for the part about Queenie
going over to the dark side.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.680
(sighs) I mean, yeah, she's cuckoo.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:33.160
But she's got a heart bigger
than this whole crazy island,

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.040
and she's so smart, you know?

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:36.800
She can legitimately read
your brain, you know,

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:37.960
she's a whatchamacallit...

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.920
-A Legilimens. -Yeah.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.640
Look... (sighs)

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.160
-(pan clangs) -You see this?

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.480
You see the pan? That's
me, I'm the pan.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:56.680
I'm all dented, dime-a-dozen.
I'm just a schmo.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:59.320
I don't know what kind of crazy
ideas you have in your head
there, lady,

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.680
but I'm sure as hell you could
do a lot better than me.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:02.880
Goodbye.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:05.240
I don't think we can, Mr. Kowalski.

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:06.480
(Jacob groans)

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.880
You could have ducked under
the counter, but you didn't.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:12.920
You could have looked the
other way, but you didn't.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.000
In fact,

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.880
you were willing to put yourself in
danger to save a perfect stranger.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:19.280
Seems to me

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:22.000
you're just the kind of average
Joe the world needs right now.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:24.320
You just don't know it yet.

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.520
That's why I had to show you.

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:31.960
We need you, Mr. Kowalski.

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:36.200
(light jazz music playing)

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:38.880
All right.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:40.800
Call me Jacob.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:41.920
Call me Lally.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.200
-Lally. -Mm.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.480
I gotta lock up.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:50.640
Thanks.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.320
Much better, Jacob.

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.320
(light jazz music continues
playing)

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:58.720
(Jacob sighs loudly)

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:04.360
I believe you know how
this works, Jacob.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:05.400
(Jacob) Mm.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.520
(magical music playing)

